  "body": "I'm using WebBluetooth API in Chrome 80 with experimental flag enabled. I can retrieved all nearby devices' info with navigator.bluetooth.requestLEScan. However, when it comes to the current device that I'm making scan from, there doesn't seem to be a way to retrieve information about it. Is there anyway that I can retrieve information of the current bluetooth device?\r\n\r\nI couldn't find anything from [here](https://developers.google.com/web/updates/2015/07/interact-with-ble-devices-on-the-web), [here](https://googlechrome.github.io/samples/web-bluetooth/), nor [here](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Bluetooth)",
